it came out  recently that uh abc picked up your  pilot acts of crime  um and i read that it's described as a  unique spin on the crime procedural  what exactly does that mean are you  allowed to say i am  in fact i'm the one that's sort of being  strict  about not saying anything so i'm not  going to tell you anything about  the show only in that the deal is i love  crime fiction one of my favorite genres  in in novels and uh in film and tv  um and um it's it's been one of the  things on my  uh checklist to my to-do list  in terms of wanting to jump in and doing  my  version of it and the thing about um the  thing about good crime fiction is is  that it's very procedural i mean  you know the enjoyment is the mystery  for  and the new story every week that you  can  kind of watch this puzzle and and these  characters try and solve this puzzle  um you know for me i feel like crime  procedurals have been kind of  on the net broadcast side um  have it's been sort of like the two or  three shows that have been around for 20  years i've been very successful they're  still on  and then outside of that um in the  streaming uh  uh in this sort of streaming universe  there's been these sort of limited  series one-offs  or even like you know continued like  anthology series like true detective  um but i just thought well with my sort  of  uh take on a crime uh procedural  where i'm sort of more on the you know  the basic cable side  to bringing that mentality or the  mentality of  uh of what those anthology or limited  series have done  and then putting and applying it to a  weekly  procedural series like you would on a  you would see on the broadcast so that's  sort of like the basic gist of it but  i'm not going to get into it more than  that  completely get it my thing about uh  broadcast television  is that i think sometimes the ideas are  really good but then they  water it down by doing 22 or 26 episodes  do you envision is this show if it gets  picked up is it 13 episodes would you  want it to be 22  is it one of these things where you  could do that many episodes and it  totally works  it is so the i first of all yes it's 22  episodes  if it gets picked up um and  i i feel you on the 22 episodes because  i feel that when i used to watch  procedurals back in the day i mean  even if you set it in a city it's like  how many murders how many exotic  murders that have these all these twists  and turns  can these detectives get um in a year  and it always ends up feeling a little  silly i remember  i would watch 24 i mean i you know i  love 24 but  you know the running joke with that is  how many crazy days does jack bauer  is jack vaughn going to have um so i did  i do address that again i'm not going to  get into it but i do address  all that and i sort of embrace that as a  sort of complication  challenge within what we're going to do  in the show i  also because i specifically went to  broadcast i didn't actually take the  project anywhere else  outside the broadcast networks because i  wanted to  embrace the commercial breaks aspect as  well  like i really think that there's an  opportunity here to tell the story where  the commercial breaks will work in my  favor in terms of how i'm going to tell  the story every week  is this something that you envisioned to  go for like many seasons  yes i mean you know it's we're following  detectives there's murder mysteries  so as long as we can keep that fresh  which i think you can crime fiction is  like one of those genres where  it's got it's pretty timeless people get  murdered all the time  whether unfortunately that's just the  way of the world and  um and fans like me love watching those  kind of mysteries so yeah i think it can  go on  it would have legs yeah

